# DRAFT citation file for TurboTab v2.0.0 (V2_DEFINITION_OF_DONE §4, "Docs: … a CITATION file").
#
# Not the repository's citation file yet. The root CITATION.cff is Classic's (Tabular ML Lab
# v1.0.0, the Streamlit app) and stays untouched on `main` (BLUEPRINT §0, §10). At the v2.0.0
# release the owner fills in every "FILL IN" below, removes the lines that stay unknown, and
# moves this file over the root CITATION.cff in the release PR.
#
# What it says: cite the paper first (preferred-citation); cite the software version you ran as
# well, because a TurboTab export's provenance record names that version (turbotab/core/export).
# Classic v1.0.0 stays citable under `references`.
#
# Format: Citation File Format 1.2.0 (https://citation-file-format.github.io/). The placeholders
# are strings, so the file stays valid YAML; a DOI is left commented out because the schema
# checks its pattern.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TurboTab in your research, please cite the paper below, and the software version you used."
type: software
title: "TurboTab"
abstract: "TurboTab, version 2 of Tabular ML Lab, takes a nutrition-research table (dietary, clinical, metabolomics, genomics or survey-instrument data) from upload to a defensible prediction or inference result. Every choice is previewed on the user's own data and recorded as a publishable sentence, and every analysis ends in an export bundle: the methods section ordered by STROBE-nut or TRIPOD+AI, the filled checklist, the participant-flow and lineage figures, and a provenance record that `python -m turbotab.replay` reproduces."
authors:
  - family-names: Hedglin
    given-names: Nolan
version: 2.0.0
# date-released: FILL IN (the date the v2.0.0 tag is pushed, YYYY-MM-DD)
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: FILL IN (the software's archived DOI, e.g. a Zenodo release DOI)
#     description: "TurboTab v2.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hedglinnolan/tabular-ml-lab"
url: "https://github.com/hedglinnolan/tabular-ml-lab"
keywords:
  - nutrition research
  - nutritional epidemiology
  - metabolomics
  - genomics
  - clinical prediction models
  - causal inference
  - reproducible research
  - modeling decision provenance
  - STROBE-nut
  - TRIPOD+AI
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "FILL IN: the paper's title"
  authors:
    - family-names: Hedglin
      given-names: Nolan
    # FILL IN: the coauthors, in the paper's order
  journal: "FILL IN: the journal (docs/audit/PR_TURBOTAB_TO_MAIN.md names an AJCN submission)"
  # year: FILL IN
  # volume: FILL IN
  # start: FILL IN
  # doi: FILL IN (the paper's DOI)
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Tabular ML Lab"
    abstract: "Classic: the released Streamlit app (Tabular ML Lab v1.0.0)."
    authors:
      - family-names: Hedglin
        given-names: Nolan
    version: 1.0.0
    date-released: 2026-09-19
    license: MIT
    repository-code: "https://github.com/hedglinnolan/tabular-ml-lab"
